    {
      "id": "I_kwDOL-xLQ88AAAABQsi7cQ",
      "title": "[op-conductor-ops] bootstrap-cluster is not idempotent when an existing cluster has an unhealthy follower",
      "author": "joshklop",
      "number": 740,
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "body": "## Summary\n\nNetchef's generated `op-conductor-bootstrap-cluster` Job is not reliably idempotent after a conductor cluster has already been formed.\n\nIf the cluster has an elected, active leader but one or more follower sequencers are temporarily unhealthy, rerunning `op-conductor-ops bootstrap-cluster` exits 1:\n\n```text\nAll sequencers are running. Bootstrapping cluster...\nERROR! Current leader is active. Please pause conductor first.\n```\n\nIt exits 0 only after every sequencer happens to become healthy:\n\n```text\nAll sequencers are running. Bootstrapping cluster...\nAll sequencers are already healthy. Skipping bootstrap.\n```\n\nThis caused Netchef's bootstrap Job to retry/fail for hours on `glamsterdam-defense-2`, despite the Raft cluster already being formed and having an active leader. No conductor reset was required; the Job eventually passed when the followers caught up.\n\n## Root cause\n\nIn `op-conductor-ops/v0.1.0`, the existing-cluster check is based on aggregate runtime health:\n\nhttps://github.com/ethereum-optimism/infra/blob/op-conductor-ops/v0.1.0/op-conductor-ops/op-conductor-ops.py#L661-L675\n\n```python\nif network_obj.is_healthy() and any(\n    sequencer.sequencer_active for sequencer in network_obj.sequencers\n):\n    typer.echo(\"All sequencers are already healthy. Skipping bootstrap.\")\n    raise typer.Exit(code=0)\n\nleader = network_obj.find_conductor_leader()\n...\nif leader.conductor_active:\n    print_error(\"Current leader is active. Please pause conductor first.\")\n    raise typer.Exit(code=1)\n```\n\n`Network.is_healthy()` requires every `conductor_sequencerHealthy` result to be true:\n\nhttps://github.com/ethereum-optimism/infra/blob/op-conductor-ops/v0.1.0/op-conductor-ops/network.py#L42-L43\n\nTransient follower health is not a durable indication of whether Raft membership has already been bootstrapped. Consequently, this valid state fails:\n\n- desired Raft membership already exists\n- leader is elected and active\n- one sequencer is actively sequencing\n- one or more followers are temporarily unhealthy/catching up\n\nThe active-leader guard is reasonable for a genuinely incomplete/destructive bootstrap. The problem is reaching it before recognizing that membership is already complete.\n\n## Evidence\n\nEnvironment:\n\n- Network: `glamsterdam-defense-2`\n- Three sequencers: `seq-0`, `seq-1`, `seq-2`\n- `op-conductor-ops/v0.1.0`\n- `op-conductor/v0.9.4`\n- Job namespace: `ps-glamsterdam-def-2-opn-reth-f-seq-0`\n\nObserved timeline:\n\n```text\n2026-09-02T07:33:19Z Conductors resumed. Bootstrap complete.\n2026-09-02T15:24:36Z All sequencers are running. Bootstrapping cluster...\n2026-09-02T15:24:36Z ERROR! Current leader is active. Please pause conductor first.\n... repeated across multiple Job pods/container retries ...\n2026-09-02T18:05:55Z All sequencers are running. Bootstrapping cluster...\n2026-09-02T18:05:55Z All sequencers are already healthy. Skipping bootstrap.\n```\n\nRetrieve the relevant Loki records with:\n\n```bash\ngcx logs query \\\n  '{namespace=\"ps-glamsterdam-def-2-opn-reth-f-seq-0\",container=\"op-conductor-ops\"} |~ \"(All sequencers are running|Current leader is active|Skipping bootstrap|Bootstrap complete|Updating cluster membership|Cluster membership updated|Conductors resumed)\"' \\\n  --from '2026-09-02T00:00:00Z' \\\n  --to '2026-09-03T00:00:00Z' \\\n  --limit 5000 -o json \\\n| jq -r '\n    [.data.result[] | .stream as $s | .values[] |\n      [(.[0] | tonumber / 1000000000 | strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")),\n       ($s.pod // \"\"), .[1]]]\n    | sort_by(.[0])[] | @tsv\n  '\n```\n\nFollower health errors during a representative failed retry:\n\n```bash\ngcx logs query \\\n  '{namespace=~\"ps-glamsterdam-def-2-opn-reth-f-seq-[0-2]\"} |~ \"(Sequencer is unhealthy|server \\\\(follower\\\\) is not healthy|unsafe head is falling behind|Current leader is active)\"' \\\n  --from '2026-09-02T17:50:00Z' \\\n  --to '2026-09-02T17:56:00Z' \\\n  --limit 5000 -o json\n```\n\nThe later retries failed before calling `update_cluster_membership`; there is no evidence of membership corruption.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nOnce desired Raft membership exists, rerunning the generated bootstrap Job should exit successfully without requiring every follower to be healthy at that instant.\n\nSuggested flow:\n\n1. Wait for conductor/sequencer RPC reachability.\n2. Query the leader's current Raft membership.\n3. Compare stable server IDs/addresses and voting status with desired membership.\n4. If membership is complete and a valid leader exists, report that the cluster is already bootstrapped and exit 0, independently of transient follower health.\n5. Enter fresh/disaster-recovery bootstrap only when membership is absent or incomplete.\n6. If membership is incomplete while a leader is active, fail safely with a membership-specific message rather than automatically pausing the leader.\n\nHealth may still be reported separately, but should not determine whether the cluster counts as bootstrapped.\n\n## Impact\n\n- Netchef deployment/health automation can remain failed while conductor itself is operational.\n- Kubernetes repeatedly retries an operation that has already achieved its desired state.\n- Operators receive misleading advice to pause a live conductor, which could cause an unnecessary sequencing interruption.\n- Unrelated follower sync or L1 availability problems are surfaced as bootstrap failures.\n",
      "createdAt": "2026-09-10T17:36:24Z",
      "closedAt": "2026-09-10T17:40:28Z",
      "state": "CLOSED",
      "commentCount": 1
    }
  ],
